A remote WebRTC `MediaStreamTrack` may not expose all constrainable properties. Because RTP does not provide some values, a track associated with an `RTCPeerConnection` will not include properties such as `facingMode` or `groupId`.[3]

`applyConstraints()` rejects when the requested constraints cannot be met, generally with an `OverconstrainedError`.[1] Constraints using `min`, `max`, or `exact` are mandatory; if any cannot be satisfied, the promise is rejected.[2]

Therefore, avoid applying camera/device-specific mandatory constraints to a remote track:

```js
try {
  await remoteTrack.applyConstraints({
    width: { ideal: 1280 },
    height: { ideal: 720 }
  });
} catch (error) {
  console.log(error.name);       // OverconstrainedError
  console.log(error.constraint); // The failing constraint, if provided
}
```

Use `getCapabilities()` and `getSettings()` to determine which properties are available before applying constraints.
